  "worked_solution": "To find the GCF, we list the factors of the coefficients and identify any common variable factors in the expressions.\n\nThe factors of $16$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,2,\\,4,\\,8,\\,16.\n$$\n\nThe factors of $24$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,4,\\,6,\\,8,\\,12,\\,24.\n$$\n\nThe common factors of $16$ and $24$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,2,\\,4,\\,8.\n$$\n\nThe greatest of these common factors is $8.$\n\nNow we look at the variable factors. Since $16$ has no variable and $24t$ contains $t,$ there are no variable factors in common.\n\nThus, the greatest common factor of $16$ and $24t$ is $8.$",
